{
  "about": "Every clause of every labelled bullet (The chain checks, Money, Refused) of every story in REGISTRY-STORIES.md, reconciled with the Lean. class: guard (the Lean decides it), omission (the Lean does not model it; the note says what the chain does instead), overrule (the Lean decides differently; the simulator follows the Lean). A guard row names a Lean declaration (decl) — stepFn, processBody, processOne, rejectOne, applyBatch, replay, a decider (reapable, rejectable, inPhase1, inPhase2) or a theorem — the arm it sits in when the declaration matches on the action or the op (arm), the exact text that entails the clause (text: inside that declaration's span, inside the arm), its kind (guard / refusal: the text is a condition — an if-conjunct or a match pattern; payment / post-state: the text is in the arm's result; no-guard: the text is the arm's pattern, which carries no signer; verdict: the declaration is a theorem), and exactly one tie: reason (a refusal name, which the core's LEAN_GUARDS table binds to the sites that refuse it — the text must be one of them) or match (a step of the story's scenario — {step} on the trunk, {branch, step} on a fork — whose action goes through that arm, or whose fold processes that op, or which exhibits that theorem's lamp). updates on a post-state row is the list of fields the arm's `with` sets, which must equal what the step changed. The scenario gate extracts the clauses from REGISTRY-STORIES.md and fails on an unclassified fragment, a clause absent from its story, a text outside its declaration or arm or part, a tie the declaration does not decide, and a decision site of the Lean no refusal name claims.",
